  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9005-1",
  "summary": "openjdk-27 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that the 2D component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause a denial of service or to read or modify sensitive data.\n(CVE-2026-91415)\n\nIt was discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91398)\n\nIt was discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-83395)\n\nIt was discovered that the Security component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-83381, CVE-2026-87294)\n\nIt was discovered that the JAXP component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-87290)\n\nIt was discovered that the JDBC component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-83387)\n\nIt was discovered that the JGSS component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\nmodify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91462)\n\nIt was discovered that the Security component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-83374)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-91410)\n\nIt was discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-87292, CVE-2026-91332, CVE-2026-91451,\nCVE-2026-91452)\n\nIt was discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-91373)\n\nIt was discovered that the JAAS component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-83380)\n\nIt was discovered that the JAXP component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-83400)\n\nIt was discovered that the JGSS component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-91463, CVE-2026-91464)\n\nIt was discovered that the Lightweight HTTP Server component of OpenJDK 27\ndid not correctly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91453)\n\nIt was discovered that the ImageIO component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-91418)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91487)\n\nIt was discovered that the Serviceability component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91374)\n\nIt was discovered that the Libraries component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authenticate users. A local attacker could possibly use this\nissue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91375)\n\nIt was discovered that the JDK tools component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authenticate users. A local attacker could possibly use this\nissue to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91379)\n\nIt was discovered that the Utility component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A local attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91380)\n\nIt was discovered that the ImageIO component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91334)\n\nIt was discovered that the JAXP component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-87367)\n\nIt was discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to modify\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-83376, CVE-2026-91461)\n\nIt was discovered that the Serviceability component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. A local attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause a denial of service or to modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91397)\n\nIt was discovered that the Sound component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause a\ndenial of service. (CVE-2026-91400)\n\nIt was discovered that the AWT component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthorize users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nsensitive data. (CVE-2026-91335)\n\nIt was discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this\nissue to read sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91394)\n\nIt was discovered that the Networking component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. An unauthenticated remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to read sensitive data. (CVE-2026-87291)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. An unauthenticated remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-83378)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. An unauthenticated remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to read sensitive data. (CVE-2026-87255)\n\nIt was discovered that the Security component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. An unauthenticated remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to read or modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91333)\n\nIt was discovered that the JSSE component of OpenJDK 27 did not correctly\nauthenticate users. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to read\nor modify sensitive data. (CVE-2026-91403)\n\nIt was discovered that the Compiler component of OpenJDK 27 did not\ncorrectly authorize users. An unauthenticated remote attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-101737)\n\nIn addition to security fixes, the updated packages contain bug fixes, new\nfeatures, and possibly incompatible changes.\n\nPlease see the following for more information:\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-10-20\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-10-21\nhttps://openjdk.org/groups/vulnerability/advisories/2026-10-24",
